<Docs title="Version Tags">
  <h1>Version Tags</h1>
  <p>
    Version tags let you label important versions with meaningful names, making it easy
    to find key milestones in your project history.
  </p>

  <h2>Available tags</h2>
  <p>MixRestore provides a curated set of tags designed for music production workflows:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Draft</strong> — work in progress, early ideas</li>
    <li><strong>Approved</strong> — signed off by collaborators or clients</li>
    <li><strong>Final</strong> — the finished version</li>
    <li><strong>Experimental</strong> — trying something risky or unusual</li>
    <li><strong>Backup</strong> — a safety checkpoint before big changes</li>
    <li><strong>Mix</strong> — a specific mix iteration</li>
    <li><strong>Milestone</strong> — a significant point in the project's development</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Adding a tag</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>In the version history, hover over the version you want to tag</li>
    <li>Click the tag icon that appears</li>
    <li>Select a tag from the dropdown menu</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Tags appear as colored pills next to the version entry. Each tag type has a distinct color
    for quick visual identification.
  </p>

  <h2>Removing a tag</h2>
  <p>
    Click the tag pill on a version to remove it. Tags can be freely added and removed
    without affecting the version content.
  </p>

  <h2>Filtering by tag</h2>
  <p>
    When your project has many versions, you can filter the history to show only
    tagged versions. This is useful for jumping between key milestones without
    scrolling through dozens of auto-saved versions.
  </p>
</Docs>
